{{ comp.tabbedCode({ tabs: [
  {
    label: "A checkout with a real refund path",
    lang: "ts",
    code: "import { defineSaga, sagaCompensate, send } from '@netscript/plugin-sagas-core';\nimport type { SagaCorrelationKey } from '@netscript/plugin-sagas-core';\n\ntype Checkout = { status: 'pending' | 'paid' };\ntype Failure = { orderId: string; reason: string };\ntype CheckoutEvent =\n  | { type: 'payment.captured'; payload: { orderId: string } }\n  | { type: 'inventory.failed'; payload: Failure };\n\nconst checkout = defineSaga('checkout')\n  .state<Checkout>({ status: 'pending' })\n  .correlate<CheckoutEvent>((event) => event.payload.orderId as SagaCorrelationKey)\n  .on<'payment.captured', { orderId: string }>(\n    'payment.captured',\n    (saga, event) => {\n      saga.state.status = 'paid';\n      return [send('inventory.reserve', { orderId: event.payload.orderId })];\n    },\n  )\n  .on<'inventory.failed', Failure>('inventory.failed', (_saga, event) => [\n    sagaCompensate(\n      { type: 'payment.captured', payload: { orderId: event.payload.orderId } },\n      event.payload.reason,\n    ),\n  ])\n  .compensate<'payment.captured', { orderId: string }>(\n    'payment.captured',\n    (_saga, event) => [send('payment.refund', { orderId: event.payload.orderId })],\n  )\n  .build();"
  }
] }) }}

<p class="ns-lede">
Both events correlate by <code>orderId</code>. When <code>inventory.failed</code> arrives, its
handler returns a compensation request for <code>payment.captured</code>. A saga bus bridge
configured with a compensator resolves that request, and a durable store records progress across
restarts. With those runtime pieces in place, the registered handler emits
<code>payment.refund</code>.
<a href="{{ '/durable-workflows/' |> url }}">See the durability model</a>.
</p>

